From 4b527a681b5fe17abae3df80fb7a05aa57ef7d53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:33:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TileLang V4.1: name every kernel after what it computes

TileLang names a CUDA kernel after its prim_func, and most of ours were
called main, so every profile and SASS dump showed main_kernel and kernels
had to be told apart by grid. Each prim_func now carries its factory's
name (packed_vocab_projection_kernel, mhc_project_streams_kernel,
moe_combine_kernel, ...). Only the symbol changes; the generated code and
the results are the same.
